{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.faddeevPhi_unique_of_pentagon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.faddeevPhi_unique_of_pentagon","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L218-L238","doc":"**Conditional Faddeev–Volkov uniqueness.** Assuming pentagon rigidity\n(`PentagonRigidity`, the open input) for a reference `Φ`, any two nowhere-zero\n`FaddeevPhi` solutions that agree at a single normalization point `z₀` are\n**equal** everywhere. Genuine derivation: rigidity gives `Φ₁ = c₁·Φ`, `Φ₂ = c₂·Φ`;\nthe normalization at `z₀` (with `Φ z₀ ≠ 0`) forces `c₁ = c₂`; hence `Φ₁ = Φ₂`.\n\nThis proves the *implication* — the pentagon (via `uniqueUpToScalar`) is an\nexplicit hypothesis, not a proved fact. It converts the keystone into rigidity:\nthe datum is forced by pentagon + normalization, not fitted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonRigidity.uniqueUpToScalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonRigidity.uniqueUpToScalar","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L215-L215","doc":"**Rigidity up to scalar** — the pentagon's Faddeev–Volkov content (open). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonRigidity.nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonRigidity.nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L213-L213","doc":"The reference solution is nowhere zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonRigidity.hb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonRigidity.hb","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L211-L211","doc":"`Re b > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonRigidity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonRigidity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L209-L209","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonRigidity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonRigidity","kind":"structure","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L203-L216","doc":"**Pentagon-rigidity datum (§3b, open input).** For a fixed nowhere-zero\n`FaddeevPhi` reference solution `Φ` at `b`, the field `uniqueUpToScalar` records\nFaddeev–Volkov rigidity: any `FaddeevPhi` solution is a *constant* multiple of\n`Φ`. This is the analytic content the pentagon / five-term relation supplies\n(Faddeev–Kashaev); it is **not** proved here — the Liouville step is the open\ninput. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.ratio_ibinv_periodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.ratio_ibinv_periodic","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L171-L191","doc":"**Dual ratio `i/b`-periodicity** (modular-dual companion of\n`ratio_ib_periodic`). For two `FaddeevPhi` solutions at the same `b`, the ratio\n`Φ₁/Φ₂` is invariant under the full `i/b`-shift wherever the shared dual\nquasi-period prefactor is nonzero.\n\nTogether with `ratio_ib_periodic` (invariance under `ib`) this proves the\ninter-solution ambiguity `Φ₁/Φ₂` is **doubly periodic** for the lattice\n`⟨ib, i/b⟩` — the exact structural input the Faddeev–Volkov (Liouville) step\nconsumes to force `uniqueUpToScalar`. This sharpens `PentagonRigidity`'s open\nfield: the remaining gap is *precisely* \"doubly-periodic ⇒ constant\", which\nadditionally needs holomorphicity/continuity of the ratio (NOT carried by the\n`FaddeevPhi` conjecture-class, which axiomatizes only the difference equations)\nand Mathlib's absent elliptic-function boundedness — see §4. Nothing here\ncloses that gap; this only makes the double-periodicity explicit and proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.phi_binv_quasiperiod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.phi_binv_quasiperiod","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L158-L169","doc":"**Dual quasi-periodicity under the full `i/b`-shift** (the `1/b`-shift applied\nat `z + i/(2b)`), guarded off the dual pole lattice — the modular-dual companion\nof `phi_b_quasiperiod`:\n`Φ_b(z) = (1 + e^{2π(z + i/(2b))/b})·Φ_b(z + i/b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.ratio_ib_periodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.ratio_ib_periodic","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L147-L156","doc":"**Ratio `ib`-periodicity.** For two `FaddeevPhi` solutions at the same `b`,\nthe ratio `Φ₁/Φ₂` is invariant under the full `ib`-shift wherever the shared\nquasi-period prefactor is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.solution_periodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.solution_periodic","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L127-L133","doc":"**Cyclic periodicity of a solution.** Given the pentagon closure, any solution\nof the recursion is `N`-periodic — it descends to a genuine function on the\ncyclic lattice `ℤ/N`. Uses `closure` essentially. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonClosure.closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonClosure.closure","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L125-L125","doc":"Full-period product trivialises — the cyclotomic-collapse / pentagon\nclosure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonClosure.period","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonClosure.period","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L122-L122","doc":"`N`-periodicity of the multiplier family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonClosure.w","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonClosure.w","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L120-L120","doc":"Shift multipliers of the finite cyclic quantum dilogarithm. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonClosure.N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonClosure.N","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L118-L118","doc":"Cyclic order (the `N` of `ζ_N`; `N = 5` is Bring's tetraplectic modulus). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonClosure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonClosure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L116-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonClosure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.PentagonClosure","kind":"structure","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L113-L125","doc":"**Pentagon closure datum.** The finite consequence of the pentagon at `ζ_N`:\n`N`-periodic multipliers whose full-period product is `1`. Honest open\nhypothesis (the operator pentagon itself is not formalised here). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.solution_unique_of_seed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.solution_unique_of_seed","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L95-L103","doc":"**Finite cyclic Faddeev–Volkov rigidity (seed uniqueness).** Two solutions of\nthe same finite multiplicative shift recursion that agree at the seed agree\neverywhere. This is the finite-lattice heart of the uniqueness statement — no\nopen input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.solution_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.solution_shift","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L84-L93","doc":"**Shifted product form.** `f (k + m)` is `f k` times the product of the `m`\nmultipliers starting at `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.solution_eq_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicDilogPentagon.solution_eq_prod","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicDilogPentagon.lean#L74-L82","doc":"**Explicit product form.** A solution of the multiplicative shift recursion is\nits seed times the partial product of the multipliers. ","signatureChunk":0}]}